{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":4366,"output":1079,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":5445,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"The tests passed! The implementation seems correct and satisfies the requirements.\nI'll do one more check on the code I wrote.\n\n```python\nimport csv\nimport io\n\ndef summarize_expenses(csv_text):\n    \"\"\"Total the amount column per category.\n\n    Returns {category: total} with each total rounded to 2 decimals.\n    Category keys are lowercase with surrounding whitespace stripped.\n    Amounts may be quoted and may use $ and thousands separators.\n    An amount wrapped in parentheses is negative, accounting style.\n    Rows with a missing or empty amount are skipped, as are blank lines.\n    \"\"\"\n    totals = {}\n    f = io.StringIO(csv_text.strip())\n    reader = csv.reader(f)\n    \n    try:\n        header = next(reader)\n    except StopIteration:\n        return {}\n\n    for row in reader:\n        if not row or len(row) < 3:\n            continue\n        \n        cat_str = row[1].strip().lower()\n        amount_str = row[2].strip()\n        \n        if not amount_str:\n            continue\n            \n        # Handle accounting style negative numbers (parentheses)\n        if amount_str.startswith('(') and amount_str.endswith(')'):\n            amount_str = '-' + amount_str[1:-1].strip()\n            \n        # Remove $ and ,\n        amount_str = amount_str.replace('$', '').replace(',', '')\n        \n        try:\n            amount = float(amount_str)\n        except ValueError:\n            continue\n            \n        totals[cat_str] = totals.get(cat_str, 0) + amount\n\n    return {cat: round(total, 2) for cat, total in totals.items()}\n```\n\nWait, one minor issue: `csv_text.strip()` might remove leading/trailing blank lines, but `csv.reader` on `io.StringIO(csv_text.s